 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Decidir hacer algo",
    "@en": "Decide to do something"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**-기로 하다** expresa una decisión o acuerdo de hacer algo: 가다 → **가기로 했어요** (decidí/decidimos ir), 먹다 → **먹기로 했어요**, 하다 → **하기로 했어요**. La forma con 했어요 sitúa la decisión antes del momento actual; el sujeto y si la decisión fue individual o grupal se entienden por el contexto.",
     "@en": "**-기로 하다** expresses a decision or agreement to do something: 가다 → **가기로 했어요** (decided / decided to go), 먹다 → **먹기로 했어요**, 하다 → **하기로 했어요**. The shape with 했어요 places the decision before the present time; the subject and whether the decision was individual or group are understood by context."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Decisión previa y compromiso",
    "@en": "Previous decision and commitment"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**-기로 했어요** informa de una decisión ya tomada, individual o compartida: **친구하고 만나기로 했어요** (quedé con un amigo). **-(으)ㄹ게요** suele comunicar el compromiso/disposición del hablante en relación con el interlocutor: **제가 전화할게요** (yo te llamaré).",
     "@en": "**-기로 했어요** reports a decision already made, individual or shared: **친구하고 만나기로 했어요** (I stayed with a friend). **-(으)ㄹ게요** usually communicates the commitment / disposition of the speaker in relation to the interlocutor: **제가 전화할게요** (I will call you)."
    }
   ]
  },
